  "question": {
    ":question/id": "2eb6d09d-7357-5a52-ac77-aa62316f0855",
    ":question/problem": "Let $a = ⟨ - 7, 15⟩$ and $b = ⟨14,-11⟩$. Find $a - 3b$.",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
    ":question/worked-solution": "To compute $a - 3b$, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na - 3b &= ⟨-7,15⟩ - 3\\cdot ⟨14,-11⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨-7,15⟩ - ⟨42,-33⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨-7 - 42, 15 - (-33)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨-49,48⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
